research/audit/wave10-certifier-tasks/lem-integral-elementary-bounds.md-15-title: "If $m \\le f \\le M$ on $[a,b]$ then $m(b-a) \\le L(f,P) \\le \\underline{\\int_a^b} f \\le \\overline{\\int_a^b} f \\le U(f,P) \\le M(b-a)$ for every partition $P$; in particular every constant function is integrable, with $\\int_a^b c = c(b-a)$"
